  <constraints>
    <constraint type="architecture">The compilation step is appended to existing document generation pipelines — it does NOT create a new pipeline. Each document generation endpoint already creates a pipeline job; the COMPILE step is added at the end.</constraint>
    <constraint type="architecture">Wiki markdown files on EC2 are the source of truth. Memgraph is a disposable query accelerator rebuilt from wiki content. The compilation step writes articles first, then syncs to Memgraph.</constraint>
    <constraint type="cost">Compilation must use the 3-step pattern: shell ($0) + agent (~$0.03-0.08) + shell (~$0.001). Total per-compilation cost under $0.10.</constraint>
    <constraint type="infrastructure">All scripts run on EC2 (t4g.small, 2GB RAM). Memgraph memory limit is 512MB. Scripts must be memory-efficient — process articles sequentially, not all in memory.</constraint>
    <constraint type="convention">Article file naming: knowledge/{phase}/{slug}.md. Code files use -- for path separators (src--components--auth.tsx.md). Non-code articles use kebab-case slug.</constraint>
    <constraint type="dependency">Requires Epic 1 complete (Memgraph, schema, wiki structure, embeddings, graph-sync) and Story 3.5 (Impact Propagation Engine).</constraint>
  </constraints>

